```

**Regulatory Parallelism** = when multiple regulators issue functionally equivalent AI governance obligations without coordination. This is the core finding of P3. Any document that shows two regulators governing the same AI function independently is evidence of parallelism.

**Governance Debt** = the compliance burden transferred to enterprises as a consequence of parallelism. Any document that quantifies compliance costs, duplication burden, or multi-regulator reporting overhead is evidence of governance debt.

**Institutional Coherence** = when governance obligations across regulators are mutually reinforcing rather than duplicative. Any document proposing coordination mechanisms, unified frameworks, or joint regulatory approaches is relevant here.

